course: dictionary
lesson: 4324
title: Reading the signs: growl
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Growl can be a verb or a noun. A growl is a low, rough, deep sound. When an animal such as a dog, bear or lion growls, it is usually giving a warning or is angry. «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.»
explain: People and body parts can growl too. A person can growl in a low, angry voice, and a stomach can growl when it is empty: «my tummy is growling». Writers often use growled instead of said to show that someone is cross.
explain: A growl is useful communication, not bad behaviour to punish. It tells you to stop, back away slowly and leave the dog alone. Never touch a dog that is growling, eating or sleeping. «A dog guarding its own garden or gate is doing a job; its growling is not about you personally.»
fact: Growl means a low, rough, deep sound made in the throat.
fact: Growled is the past form of growl, and a growl is the noun.
fact: «A dog warns before it bites: it yawns, licks its lips, turns its head away, shows the whites of its eyes, tucks its tail, freezes and then growls.»
fact: «Tasmanian devils» screech and growl to sort out who eats first.
fact: Animals use sounds like growls, barks and purrs to communicate.
exercise: «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» What is a growling dog doing? | Singing a happy song | *Giving a clear warning | Asking to be fed | Showing it wants a belly rub
exercise: «My tummy is growling.» What is making the low, rumbling noise? | *My stomach | My feet | My ears | My hair
exercise: «A dog guarding its own garden or gate is doing a job; its growling is not about you personally.» What should you do if a dog growls at you? | *Stop, do not stare, and back away slowly | Pat it on the head | Run straight at it | Stare into its eyes
test: «Writers use growled instead of said to show anger.» Why might a writer choose growled? | *To show the character is angry | To show the character is asleep | To show the character is lost | To show the character is happy
test: «Tasmanian devils screech and growl to sort out who eats first.» Why do the devils growl? | To say goodnight | To ask for help | *To sort out who eats first | To find a new home
exam: Mia sees a dog that growls and shows its teeth. What is the safest thing to do? | Shout at it to be quiet | *Stay away, back off slowly and leave it alone | Walk up and give it a hug | Throw it a biscuit
